# Kernel command line uniLoader hands to the kernel (blob/cmdline, written by
# `make uniloader` via the cmdline-blob target). One string; lines starting
# with # are dropped. @BOOT_UUID@ and @ROOT_UUID@ are filled from the rootfs
# (vendor_boot header cmdline in the rootfs chroot); the build appends
# `bootloader=uniloader` and BOOTARGS_EXTRA. The DTS /chosen/bootargs keeps
# the same tokens until uniLoader takes over the command line.
earlycon=qcom_geni,0x0099c000 console=tty0 fbcon=font:TER16x32 loglevel=4 arm-smmu.disable_bypass=0 PMOS_NO_OUTPUT_REDIRECT pmos_boot_uuid=@BOOT_UUID@ pmos_root_uuid=@ROOT_UUID@ pmos_rootfsopts=defaults
